IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hpnl-dates`
IMPORT `hpnl-notifier`

-- Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (WA) -- worked cases, from the seat of the notifier.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (mrdoc_49311, with mrdoc_49650 for the WA modifications), never copied from the encoding's
-- output. No scenario life raised this Law; the facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Every judgment of a
-- Board, a panel or a court is given as a fact.
--
-- Weekdays were worked by hand: 1 January 2026 is a Thursday; 1 January 2028 a Saturday.
--
-- A breached DEONTIC cannot be compared with EQUALS on the stable l4, so the three regulative rules are asserted
-- through CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED.

-- HYPOTHETICAL: Priya had a hip replacement at a Perth private hospital. Her surgeon, Dr Lee, has general and specialist
-- registration. She thinks the operation was done badly and that Dr Lee had been drinking.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 138-139B: can a notification be made about this person. Arguments: registration, when it happened, prior Act allowed.
`registered now` MEANS `registered now under this Law (general, specialist, provisional, limited or non-practising registration)`
`while registered` MEANS `while the person was registered`

#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered now` `while registered` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: a notification may be made about a registered health practitioner for behaviour while registered (s 138(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered now` `before the person was first registered` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: a notification may be made for behaviour before registration (s 138(1)(b)), but that behaviour cannot be unsatisfactory professional performance or unprofessional conduct (s 138(2))`
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered now` `during a gap in registration (for example after it ended, lapsed, or was suspended or cancelled)` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: a notification may be made for behaviour in a gap in registration (s 138(1)(c)); it cannot be unsatisfactory professional performance, nor unprofessional conduct except where s 139 applies (practising on after registration ended under s 108(2)(a)) (s 138(2))`
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered now as a student` `while registered` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: a notification may be made about a registered student, on the grounds in s 144(2)`
-- Dr Lee retired last year; the operation was while registered.
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered under this Law before, but not now` `while registered` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: a notification may be made about a former practitioner for behaviour while registered, as if still registered (s 139A(2)); Part 8 applies except Divisions 2 and 6 (s 139A(3))`
-- Behaviour after a former practitioner's registration ended: s 139A is silent.
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered under this Law before, but not now` `during a gap in registration (for example after it ended, lapsed, or was suspended or cancelled)` FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `section 139A reaches a former practitioner's behaviour only while the person was registered; this Law does not say what may be done about behaviour after registration ended`
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered only under a corresponding prior Act (before this Law), never under this Law` `while registered` TRUE EQUALS `answered` `yes: a notification may be made about a person registered under a corresponding prior Act for behaviour while so registered, to the extent one could have been made under that Act (s 139B(2), (3)); Part 8 applies except Divisions 2 and 7 (s 139B(4))`
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `registered only under a corresponding prior Act (before this Law), never under this Law` `while registered` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: for a person registered only under a corresponding prior Act, s 139B applies only to the extent a notification could have been made, and proceedings taken, under that Act (s 139B(3))`
#ASSERT `Can a notification be made about this person question` `never registered as a health practitioner` `while registered` TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `Part 8 speaks of a person registered under this Law, or formerly registered, or registered under a corresponding prior Act; for a person never registered see the title and practice protections and interim prohibition orders (Part 7 Division 10, Part 8 Division 7A), not encoded`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 144-145: can I make a voluntary notification. Arguments: about, (a) conduct, (b) care, (c) unsuitable, (d) impairment,
-- (e) contravened the Law, (f) condition, (g) improperly registered, student charged or convicted, maximum months.
`practitioner` MEANS `a registered health practitioner`
`student` MEANS `a registered student`
`yes practitioner ground` MEANS `answered` `yes: you may notify the National Agency, because you believe a ground in s 144(1) exists (ss 144(1), 145)`
`yes student ground` MEANS `answered` `yes: you may notify the National Agency about the student, because you believe a ground in s 144(2) exists (ss 144(2), 145)`
`no listed ground` MEANS `not covered` `section 144 does not list the matter you describe as a ground; the National Board decides in its preliminary assessment whether a notification relates to a ground (s 149(1)(b))`

-- Priya believes the care was below standard: (b).
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
-- Each other practitioner ground alone.
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes practitioner ground`
-- None believed (for example only a fee dispute): not covered.
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `practitioner` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `no listed ground`
-- A student convicted of an offence punishable by 12 months: (2)(a), the edge. 11 months: no ground of its own.
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `student` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 12 EQUALS `yes student ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `student` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 11 EQUALS `no listed ground`
-- A maximum of 24 months, but never charged: no ground.
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `student` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 24 EQUALS `no listed ground`
-- Student impairment (2)(b); student condition (2)(c).
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `student` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes student ground`
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `student` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `yes student ground`
-- Care below standard is a practitioner ground only: for a student it is not listed.
#ASSERT `Can I make a voluntary notification question` `student` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `no listed ground`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 146-147.
#ASSERT `Must Ahpra help me make my notification question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you asked, so the National Agency must give you reasonable assistance to make the notification (s 147(1))`
#ASSERT `Must Ahpra help me make my notification question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you asked, so the National Agency must give you reasonable assistance to make the notification (s 147(1))`
#ASSERT `Must Ahpra help me make my notification question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the National Agency may help you without being asked, because you cannot put it in writing without help or need help to clarify it (s 147(2)); if you ask, it must (s 147(1))`
#ASSERT `Must Ahpra help me make my notification question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not unless you ask: the National Agency must give reasonable assistance if asked (s 147(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my notification properly made question` `by telephone or in person` TRUE EQUALS `yes: a notification may be made verbally, including by telephone, and the National Agency must record it (s 146(1)(a), (3))`
#ASSERT `Is my notification properly made question` `in writing, by letter, email or online` TRUE EQUALS `yes: a notification may be made in writing, including by email or other electronic means (s 146(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is my notification properly made question` `in writing, by letter, email or online` FALSE EQUALS `not yet: a notification must include particulars of the basis on which it is made (s 146(2))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 140-143: was a notification required. Arguments: about, who knew, what it was, student risk, belief reasonable,
-- how the practitioner knew, enrolled or placed.
`in practice` MEANS `a registered health practitioner, in the course of practising their profession`
`intoxicated` MEANS `practising while intoxicated by alcohol or drugs`
`ordinary` MEANS `in ordinary practice (none of the exceptions below)`
`practitioner must notify` MEANS `answered` `yes: the practitioner had to notify the National Agency as soon as practicable after forming the reasonable belief (s 141(2)); not doing so is not an offence but may lead to action under Part 8 (s 141(3))`

-- The anaesthetist in Priya's theatre reasonably believed Dr Lee was intoxicated: s 141(2).
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `practitioner must notify`
-- Each kind of notifiable conduct (s 140(b)-(d)).
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `sexual misconduct in connection with practising the profession` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `practitioner must notify`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `an impairment placing the public at risk of substantial harm` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `practitioner must notify`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `a significant departure from accepted professional standards placing the public at risk of harm` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `practitioner must notify`
-- A poor outcome alone is not notifiable conduct.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `something else (for example a poor outcome, rudeness, or a billing dispute)` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the conduct is not notifiable conduct as s 140 defines it (a voluntary notification may still be made)`
-- A suspicion that is not a reasonable belief.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE FALSE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: a mandatory notification turns on a reasonable belief (ss 141(1), 142(1), 143(1))`
-- Learnt at a dinner party, not in practice.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `a registered health practitioner, outside the course of practising their profession` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: section 141 applies only to a belief formed in the course of practising the profession (s 141(1))`
-- The s 141(4) exceptions, each; (ca) is the WA one: Dr Lee's own GP, treating him for alcohol dependence, need not notify, even
-- of practising while intoxicated.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `while treating the other practitioner or student as their patient` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: in Western Australia a belief formed while treating the other practitioner or student is not formed in the course of practising (s 141(4)(ca), inserted by the Application Act 2024 (WA) s 27)`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `sexual misconduct in connection with practising the profession` FALSE TRUE `while treating the other practitioner or student as their patient` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: in Western Australia a belief formed while treating the other practitioner or student is not formed in the course of practising (s 141(4)(ca), inserted by the Application Act 2024 (WA) s 27)`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `working for the other practitioner's indemnity insurer, from a disclosure in a legal proceeding or legal advice under the policy` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: a belief formed working for the other practitioner's indemnity insurer from a disclosure in a legal proceeding or legal advice is not formed in the course of practising (s 141(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `giving advice for a legal proceeding or legal advice` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: a belief formed giving advice for a legal proceeding or legal advice is not formed in the course of practising (s 141(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `as a lawyer acting for the other practitioner or student` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: a belief formed as a lawyer acting for the other practitioner or student is not formed in the course of practising (s 141(4)(c))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `on a quality assurance committee whose Act forbids disclosing it` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: a belief formed on a quality assurance committee whose Act forbids disclosure is not formed in the course of practising (s 141(4)(d))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `knowing or reasonably believing Ahpra had already been notified` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: a practitioner who knows or reasonably believes the National Agency has already been notified does not form the belief in the course of practising (s 141(4)(e))`
-- The hospital, Dr Lee's employer, reasonably believed it: s 142.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `the practitioner's employer (under a contract of employment or for services)` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the employer had to notify the National Agency (s 142(1)); if the Agency learns it did not, it must report the failure to the responsible Minister, who must report it to a health complaints entity, the employer's licensing authority or another appropriate entity (s 142(2), (3))`
-- The s 141(4) exceptions are for practitioners: an employer that treats its practitioner is still bound.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `the practitioner's employer (under a contract of employment or for services)` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `while treating the other practitioner or student as their patient` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the employer had to notify the National Agency (s 142(1)); if the Agency learns it did not, it must report the failure to the responsible Minister, who must report it to a health complaints entity, the employer's licensing authority or another appropriate entity (s 142(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `student` `the practitioner's employer (under a contract of employment or for services)` `intoxicated` TRUE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: section 142 places the employer's duty only for a registered health practitioner, not a student`
-- A student on placement: the education provider (s 143) and a supervising practitioner (s 141(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `student` `the student's education provider` `intoxicated` TRUE TRUE `ordinary` TRUE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the education provider had to notify the National Agency (s 143(1)); not doing so is not an offence, but the National Board must publish details of the failure on its website (s 143(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `student` `the student's education provider` `intoxicated` TRUE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the student's education provider must notify only if the student is enrolled in its program of study or it arranged the student's clinical training (s 143(1))`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `student` `in practice` `intoxicated` TRUE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `practitioner must notify`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `student` `in practice` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the student's impairment is not one that may place the public at substantial risk of harm in clinical training (s 141(1)(b), s 143(1))`
-- A patient or a relative who knew: Division 2 is silent.
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `someone else` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `this Law does not say; Division 2 of Part 8 puts the duty to notify only on registered health practitioners, employers and education providers`
#ASSERT `Was a notification required question` `practitioner` `the student's education provider` `intoxicated` FALSE TRUE `ordinary` TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `this Law does not say; Division 2 of Part 8 puts the duty to notify only on registered health practitioners, employers and education providers`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 149: the 60 days, Schedule 7 cl 31(2), (3).
-- Received Thursday 5 March 2026: day 60 is Monday 4 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the Board assess my notification question` (`the day` 5 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 4 5 2026
-- Received Monday 2 March 2026: day 60 is Friday 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the Board assess my notification question` (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 1 5 2026
-- Received Tuesday 3 March 2026: day 60 is Saturday 2 May, so Monday 4 May (cl 31(3)). Received 4 March: Sunday 3 May, so 4 May.
#ASSERT `By when must the Board assess my notification question` (`the day` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 4 5 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the Board assess my notification question` (`the day` 4 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 4 5 2026
-- Received Friday 31 December 2027: 31 days of January and 29 of February 2028 (a leap year) make Tuesday 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `By when must the Board assess my notification question` (`the day` 31 12 2027) EQUALS `the day` 29 2 2028
-- In time on the last day; late the day after.
#ASSERT `Was my notification assessed in time question` (`the day` 5 3 2026) (`the day` 4 5 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my notification assessed in time question` (`the day` 5 3 2026) (`the day` 5 5 2026))
#ASSERT `Was my notification assessed in time question` (`the day` 3 3 2026) (`the day` 4 5 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my notification assessed in time question` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 4 5 2026))

-- The s 149 rule. Received 5 March 2026: 60 days. Received 3 March 2026: 62 days (to Monday 4 May).
`assessed on day 60` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 149 assessment duty for a notification received on` (`the day` 5 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the National Board` `conduct the preliminary assessment of the notification (s 149(1))` 60))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `assessed on day 60` EQUALS TRUE
`assessed on day 61` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 149 assessment duty for a notification received on` (`the day` 5 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the National Board` `conduct the preliminary assessment of the notification (s 149(1))` 61))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `assessed on day 61` EQUALS FALSE
`assessed on day 62 after a weekend` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 149 assessment duty for a notification received on` (`the day` 3 3 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the National Board` `conduct the preliminary assessment of the notification (s 149(1))` 62))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `assessed on day 62 after a weekend` EQUALS TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 150: the health complaints entity. Arguments: where, also a complaint ground, about a practitioner.
#ASSERT `Will the other body be told question` `with Ahpra (a notification under this Law)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the National Board must, as soon as practicable, tell the health complaints entity and give it a copy and any other relevant information (s 150(1)); the two must try to agree how it is dealt with, and if they cannot, the most serious action either proposes must be taken (s 150(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Will the other body be told question` `with Ahpra (a notification under this Law)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 150(1) applies only if the subject matter would also be a ground for a complaint to a health complaints entity`
#ASSERT `Will the other body be told question` `with a health complaints entity (in Western Australia, the Health and Disability Services Complaints Office)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the health complaints entity must, as soon as practicable, tell the National Board and give it a copy and any other relevant information (s 150(2)); the two must try to agree how it is dealt with, and if they cannot, the most serious action either proposes must be taken (s 150(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Will the other body be told question` `with a health complaints entity (in Western Australia, the Health and Disability Services Complaints Office)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 150(2) applies to a complaint about a health practitioner (an individual who practises a health profession)`

-- s 151: no further action. Arguments: (a), (b), (c) not registered, (c) not in public interest, (d), (e), (f) remedied,
-- (f) no more needed.
`may stop` MEANS `yes: the Board may decide to take no further action (s 151(1)); if it does, it must tell you in writing, with its reason (s 151(3), (4)), and it may still take your notification into account later as part of a pattern (s 151(2))`
`may not stop` MEANS `no: section 151 lets the Board take no further action only if one of its grounds holds (s 151(1)(a)-(f))`
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may stop`
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may stop`
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may stop`
-- (c) needs both limbs: no longer registered, but in the public interest to go on.
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may not stop`
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may stop`
-- Priya's complaint is also with HaDSCO and the Board referred it there: (e).
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may stop`
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `may stop`
-- (f) needs both: Dr Lee apologised and retrained, but the Board thinks more is needed.
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `may not stop`
#ASSERT `Can the Board take no further action question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may not stop`

-- s 152: telling the practitioner.
#ASSERT `Will the practitioner be told question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the National Board must, as soon as practicable, tell the practitioner or student in writing about the notification and its nature (s 152(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Will the practitioner be told question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not necessarily: the Board is not required to tell the practitioner or student, because it reasonably believes doing so would prejudice an investigation or put a person at risk (s 152(3))`
#ASSERT `Will the practitioner be told question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not necessarily: the Board is not required to tell the practitioner or student, because it reasonably believes doing so would prejudice an investigation or put a person at risk (s 152(3))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 159A-192: what I am told later.
#ASSERT `What must I be told about the decision question` `the Board took immediate action (for example suspended the practitioner or imposed conditions) (s 156)` EQUALS `the Board may tell you of the decision and its reasons, but need not (s 159A(2))`
#ASSERT `What must I be told about the decision question` `the Board decided what to do after an investigation (s 167)` EQUALS `the Board may tell you of the decision and its reasons, but need not (s 167A(2))`
#ASSERT `What must I be told about the decision question` `the Board decided what to do after a health or performance assessment report (s 177)` EQUALS `the Board may tell you of the decision and its reasons, but need not (s 177A(2))`
#ASSERT `What must I be told about the decision question` `the Board took action after the show cause process (caution, undertaking, conditions, reprimand and the like) (s 179(2))` EQUALS `the Board must give you written notice of the decision as soon as practicable; it may also give the reasons (s 180(1)(b), (2))`
#ASSERT `What must I be told about the decision question` `a health panel or performance and professional standards panel decided the matter (s 191 or s 191A)` EQUALS `the Board must give you written notice of the panel's decision within 30 days after the panel makes it; it may also give the reasons (s 192(2)(b), (4))`
#ASSERT `What must I be told about the decision question` `the Board decided to investigate (s 160)` EQUALS `the Board must give you written notice of the progress of the investigation at not less than 3 monthly intervals (s 161(3)(b)); the exceptions in s 161(4) cover only notices to the practitioner or student`
-- s 161(3): decided to investigate Monday 16 March 2026: 3 months on is Tuesday 16 June 2026. Decided Monday 30 November 2026:
-- 3 months on is 28 February 2027 (no 30 February), a Sunday, so Monday 1 March 2027. Decided Saturday 21 February 2026:
-- 21 May 2026 is a Thursday.
#ASSERT `By when must I next hear of the investigation question` (`the day` 16 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 16 6 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I next hear of the investigation question` (`the day` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I next hear of the investigation question` (`the day` 21 2 2026) EQUALS `the day` 21 5 2026
-- s 192(2): panel decides Wednesday 10 June 2026: day 30 is Friday 10 July 2026. Decides 11 June: day 30 is Saturday 11 July,
-- so Monday 13 July.
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of the panel decision question` (`the day` 10 6 2026) EQUALS `the day` 10 7 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of the panel decision question` (`the day` 11 6 2026) EQUALS `the day` 13 7 2026
`told on day 32 after a weekend` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 192 notice duty for a panel decision on` (`the day` 11 6 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the National Board` `give the notifier written notice of the panel's decision (s 192(2)(b))` 32))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `told on day 32 after a weekend` EQUALS TRUE
`told on day 33` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 192 notice duty for a panel decision on` (`the day` 11 6 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the National Board` `give the notifier written notice of the panel's decision (s 192(2)(b))` 33))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `told on day 33` EQUALS FALSE
-- Notice of something else does not count.
`told something else` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 192 notice duty for a panel decision on` (`the day` 10 6 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the National Board` `conduct the preliminary assessment of the notification (s 149(1))` 5))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `told something else` EQUALS FALSE

-- s 187: submissions.
#ASSERT `Can I make a submission to the panel question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: as the notifier you may make a submission to the panel about the matter, with the panel's leave (s 187); the hearing is not open to the public (s 189)`
#ASSERT `Can I make a submission to the panel question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not without the panel's leave: a notifier may make a submission only with the leave of the panel (s 187)`
#ASSERT `Can I make a submission to the panel question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 187 lets the notifier make a submission only where the matter relates to the notification`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 129-130: insurance. Arguments: registration type, practising, compliant cover.
`practising registration` MEANS `practising registration (general, specialist, provisional or limited)`
#ASSERT `Did the practitioner have to be insured question` `practising registration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: they must not practise unless appropriate professional indemnity insurance arrangements are in force (s 129(1)); they had them`
-- Dr Lee's cover had lapsed when he operated.
#ASSERT `Did the practitioner have to be insured question` `practising registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, and they were not: practising without appropriate professional indemnity insurance arrangements breaches s 129(1); it is not an offence but may lead to health, conduct or performance action (s 129(4)), and you may notify on that ground (s 144(1)(e))`
#ASSERT `Did the practitioner have to be insured question` `practising registration` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 129 does not apply while the practitioner is not practising the profession`
#ASSERT `Did the practitioner have to be insured question` `non-practising registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 129 does not apply to non-practising registration (s 129(5)); a practitioner with non-practising registration must not practise at all (s 75)`
#ASSERT `Did the practitioner have to be insured question` `student registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 129 applies to a registered health practitioner, which by definition excludes registration as a student (s 5)`
#ASSERT `Did the practitioner have to be insured question` `not registered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 129 applies only to a registered health practitioner (s 5)`
-- s 130: aware Saturday 31 October 2026: day 7 is Saturday 7 November, so Monday 9 November. Aware Monday 2 November: day 7
-- is Monday 9 November.
#ASSERT `By when must the practitioner report lapsed insurance question` (`the day` 31 10 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the practitioner report lapsed insurance question` (`the day` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the practitioner report lapsed insurance question` (`the day` 3 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 10 11 2026
`reported on day 9` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 130 insurance notice duty from` (`the day` 31 10 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the registered health practitioner` `give the National Board written notice that indemnity insurance is no longer in place (s 130(1))` 9))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `reported on day 9` EQUALS TRUE
`reported on day 8 from a Monday` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 130 insurance notice duty from` (`the day` 2 11 2026)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the registered health practitioner` `give the National Board written notice that indemnity insurance is no longer in place (s 130(1))` 8))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `reported on day 8 from a Monday` EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 237: protection from liability.
#ASSERT `Am I protected from liability question` `made a notification` TRUE EQUALS `yes: you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process for it, it is not a breach of professional ethics, and you incur no liability for defamation (s 237(1)-(3))`
#ASSERT `Am I protected from liability question` `gave information in an investigation, or for another purpose under this Law, to a person exercising functions under it` TRUE EQUALS `yes: you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process for it, it is not a breach of professional ethics, and you incur no liability for defamation (s 237(1)-(3))`
-- Priya's husband, who told her what he saw: s 237(4)(a).
#ASSERT `Am I protected from liability question` `gave the notifier the information the notification was based on` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the protection extends to you (s 237(4)): you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process, it is not a breach of professional ethics, and you incur no liability for defamation`
#ASSERT `Am I protected from liability question` `was otherwise concerned in making the notification or giving the information` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the protection extends to you (s 237(4)): you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process, it is not a breach of professional ethics, and you incur no liability for defamation`
#ASSERT `Am I protected from liability question` `made a notification` FALSE EQUALS `no: section 237 protects only what is done in good faith`
#ASSERT `Am I protected from liability question` `gave the notifier the information the notification was based on` FALSE EQUALS `no: section 237 protects only what is done in good faith`

-- s 237A: reprisals. Arguments: my action, good faith, what was done, because of it, the day.
`notifying` MEANS `making a notification`
`helping` MEANS `giving information, documents or other assistance to Ahpra, a Board or an investigator`
`sacked` MEANS `I was dismissed, or refused employment`
`threatened` MEANS `threats or intimidation to persuade me not to notify or help`
`other detriment` MEANS `some other detriment or reprisal (for example being refused treatment, sued, or demoted)`
-- Priya, a nurse at the same hospital, is dismissed on Monday 1 December 2025, the day s 237A commenced, for notifying.
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `notifying` TRUE `sacked` TRUE (`the day` 1 12 2025) EQUALS `answered` `yes: dismissing or refusing to employ a person because, or in the belief that, they took or intend to take protected action is an offence (s 237A(1)(b))`
-- The day before: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `notifying` TRUE `sacked` TRUE (`the day` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `not covered` `section 237A commenced on 1 December 2025; earlier conduct falls under the Law as it stood before then, which is not deposited`
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `notifying` TRUE `sacked` FALSE (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `answered` `no: section 237A(1)(b) and (c) apply only where it was done because, or in the belief that, you took or intended to take protected action`
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `notifying` TRUE `other detriment` TRUE (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `answered` `yes: subjecting a person to other detriment or reprisal because, or in the belief that, they took or intend to take protected action is an offence (s 237A(1)(c))`
-- Threats need no "because": (a) is about persuading a person not to act.
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `notifying` TRUE `threatened` FALSE (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `answered` `yes: using threats or intimidation to try to persuade a person not to take protected action is an offence (s 237A(1)(a))`
-- A notification not in good faith is not protected action.
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `notifying` FALSE `sacked` TRUE (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `answered` `no: a notification is protected action only if made in good faith (s 237A(2))`
-- Giving information is protected action without a good faith condition (s 237A(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Is it a reprisal offence question` `helping` FALSE `sacked` TRUE (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `answered` `yes: dismissing or refusing to employ a person because, or in the belief that, they took or intend to take protected action is an offence (s 237A(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `What is the maximum reprisal penalty question` `an individual` EQUALS 60000
#ASSERT `What is the maximum reprisal penalty question` `a body corporate (for example a hospital company or a practice company)` EQUALS 120000

-- s 237B(1): the clause. Arguments: restricts disclosure about a practitioner, my action, good faith.
-- Priya settles her negligence claim; the deed has a confidentiality clause covering Dr Lee's care.
#ASSERT `Can my agreement stop me notifying question` TRUE `notifying` TRUE EQUALS `no: the clause is void to the extent it prevents or limits you from making a notification in good faith (s 237B(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my agreement stop me notifying question` TRUE `helping` FALSE EQUALS `no: the clause is void to the extent it prevents or limits you from giving information, documents or other assistance to a person exercising functions under this Law (s 237B(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can my agreement stop me notifying question` TRUE `notifying` FALSE EQUALS `section 237B does not make it void for a notification not made in good faith (s 237B(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can my agreement stop me notifying question` FALSE `notifying` TRUE EQUALS `section 237B does not make it void: the agreement is not a non-disclosure agreement as s 237B(3) defines it (it must restrict disclosure about the health, conduct or performance of a registered or former registered health practitioner)`

-- s 237B(2): the offence. Arguments: restricts, other party, who, carve-out, the day entered into.
`a hospital` MEANS `a health service provider whose services are provided by registered health practitioners (for example a hospital or clinic)`
`a company` MEANS `a body corporate (for example a hospital company or a practice company)`
-- The hospital (a company) signs on 1 December 2025 with no carve-out: offence, $10,000.
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `a hospital` `a company` FALSE (`the day` 1 12 2025))'s `the most it can be fined` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `a hospital` `a company` FALSE (`the day` 1 12 2025))'s `the offence answer` EQUALS `yes: a relevant person must not enter into a non-disclosure agreement that does not clearly set out in writing that it does not limit notifications or giving information (s 237B(2)); the most it can be fined is shown`
-- Dr Lee personally: $5,000.
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `the practitioner, or another registered health practitioner` `an individual` FALSE (`the day` 2 3 2026))'s `the most it can be fined` EQUALS 5000
-- Signed 30 November 2025: before s 237B(2).
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `a hospital` `a company` FALSE (`the day` 30 11 2025))'s `the offence answer` EQUALS `no: section 237B(2) commenced on 1 December 2025; it does not reach an agreement entered into before then`
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `a hospital` `a company` FALSE (`the day` 30 11 2025))'s `the most it can be fined` EQUALS 0
-- With the carve-out: no offence.
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `an employer or former employer of a registered or formerly registered health practitioner` `a company` TRUE (`the day` 2 3 2026))'s `the offence answer` EQUALS `no: the agreement clearly sets out in writing that it does not limit notifications or giving information, as s 237B(2) requires`
-- Only the indemnity insurer signed with Priya: not a relevant person.
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` TRUE `none of these (for example only an insurer, or a person who is not a practitioner)` `a company` FALSE (`the day` 2 3 2026))'s `the offence answer` EQUALS `no: section 237B(2) binds only a relevant person (s 237B(3)): a practitioner, a practitioner's employer or former employer, or a health service provider using registered practitioners`
#ASSERT (`Did they commit the NDA offence question` FALSE `a hospital` `a company` FALSE (`the day` 2 3 2026))'s `the offence answer` EQUALS `no: the agreement is not a non-disclosure agreement as s 237B(3) defines it`
